const PLAN = {"destination":{"fileKey":"tN2AM7RZD2InF1LYnN0zcn","pageId":"5:422"},"status":"planned","introduction":"Internal evidence collection for Essentials 2.0 / LearningSpace. Directory-first research into university-managed identity, provisioning and recovery, with Canvas as a complementary course-membership source and CSV/manual routes for institutional exceptions. Product screenshots are observed examples or analogies; official documentation establishes specific technical behavior. All adaptations are proposals to validate.","ownershipHypothesis":"University identity infrastructure supplies institutional identity and sign-in; Canvas supplies relevant course memberships and roles; LearningSpace controls local access rules, guests and product-specific information. Validate with university IT.","synthesis":{"patterns":["Separate the IT connection task from everyday user administration. Configuration guidance, attribute mapping, scoped groups and a dry run make the intended population and data transfer reviewable before enabling provisioning.","Treat institutional sign-in, creating a user record and linking an existing record as distinct events. Establish a durable institutional identifier and make mismatches recoverable. A successful login can still leave a person without application or course access.","Expose the source of managed fields and group membership, and explain where changes must be made. Keep course roles scoped to their course; an imported teacher role is not institutional administrator authority.","Show connection health and per-record outcomes separately. A failed sync is not evidence that users departed. Guard unusually large removals and distinguish suspending access, removing membership and deleting records.","Use the Canvas Provisioning export as a concrete data-source scenario, then separate upload, mapping, validation, preview and completion. Repeat imports need stable identifiers and explicit update rules. A file import remains a snapshot until a separate recurring process exists.","Canvas roster mechanisms establish a feasible membership source, subject to institution configuration and authorization. Match roster identities to existing users before applying course-scoped roles and enrollment changes."],"gaps":["Library coverage is thin for actual LDAP setup, identifier collisions, externally managed fields and sync failures. Official documentation supplies technical evidence; screenshots of analogous SaaS interactions do not establish LearningSpace behavior.","No available screenshot or API establishes institutional permission to share personal data. Validate purpose, fields, roles, retention and operational responsibilities with university IT.","Guest identity, changed institutional identifiers, person merges and effective access across multiple courses require institution-specific validation.","Board sequences may select at most eight original steps. The report retains every collected step, including end states; documented omissions are in board-plan.json."],"questionsForIT":["What is authoritative for people, sign-in, institutional affiliation, and course enrollment today?","Which non-recycled identifier survives email changes and returning-user scenarios across systems?","How can IT scope a pilot population and review exactly which fields leave each source?","Which administrators can authorize connectors, export Canvas reports and approve imports?","What should happen when sign-in succeeds but no LearningSpace entitlement or course membership exists?","How are guests, visiting faculty, alumni and temporary exceptions represented and reviewed?","Which departure events disable the account, remove one membership, or trigger historical retention decisions?","What latency, monitoring, credential-renewal ownership and support escalation are required?","Which local overrides are permitted, and how should source changes interact with them?","What institutional privacy review and agreements authorize the selected population and data fields?"]},"layout":{"PAD":60,"STICKY_W":280,"STICKY_H":240,"IMG_X":620,"IMG_W":280,"IMG_GAP":16,"LABEL_H":74,"ROW_GAP":80,"TOP":500},"sections":[{"id":"Q1","nodeId":null,"title":"How does university IT connect and scope institutional identity?","answer":"Separate the IT connection task from everyday user administration. Configuration guidance, attribute mapping, scoped groups and a dry run make the intended population and data transfer reviewable before enabling provisioning.","openQuestions":["Which identity systems and LDAP/Active Directory environments do participating universities operate?","Who owns the connection, and which groups and attributes may LearningSpace receive?","Is access assigned separately from account creation?"],"x":0,"y":600,"width":2300,"height":3742},{"id":"Q2","nodeId":null,"title":"How do existing university users arrive and link to the right account?","answer":"Treat institutional sign-in, creating a user record and linking an existing record as distinct events. Establish a durable institutional identifier and make mismatches recoverable. A successful login can still leave a person without application or course access.","openQuestions":["Which immutable identifier survives email and affiliation changes?","What evidence permits linking an existing local account? Who resolves collisions?","What separate route should guests and external faculty use?"],"x":2480,"y":600,"width":2300,"height":2903},{"id":"Q3","nodeId":null,"title":"How are externally managed people, groups, and permissions represented?","answer":"Expose the source of managed fields and group membership, and explain where changes must be made. Keep course roles scoped to their course; an imported teacher role is not institutional administrator authority.","openQuestions":["Which fields and permissions can administrators override locally?","Can a person be faculty in one course and a learner in another?","How will the interface explain effective access from multiple sources?"],"x":4960,"y":600,"width":2300,"height":2552},{"id":"Q4","nodeId":null,"title":"What happens when users or connections change?","answer":"Show connection health and per-record outcomes separately. A failed sync is not evidence that users departed. Guard unusually large removals and distinguish suspending access, removing membership and deleting records.","openQuestions":["What grace period and escalation route apply when provisioning fails?","What happens to recordings, history and audit trails when someone leaves?","Can returning users recover the same identity and course history?"],"x":7440,"y":600,"width":2300,"height":2988},{"id":"Q5","nodeId":null,"title":"How can administrators safely import and update users in bulk?","answer":"Use the Canvas Provisioning export as a concrete data-source scenario, then separate upload, mapping, validation, preview and completion. Repeat imports need stable identifiers and explicit update rules. A file import remains a snapshot until a separate recurring process exists.","openQuestions":["Who may export from Canvas and import into LearningSpace?","Which identifiers are available, and how will rows match existing accounts?","Should valid rows proceed when other rows fail, and what downloadable error report is required?"],"x":9920,"y":600,"width":3048,"height":2597},{"id":"Q6","nodeId":null,"title":"How can Canvas complement university identity without creating duplicate users?","answer":"Canvas roster mechanisms establish a feasible membership source, subject to institution configuration and authorization. Match roster identities to existing users before applying course-scoped roles and enrollment changes.","openQuestions":["Which Canvas integration and permissions are available at each institution?","How do Canvas identifiers map to the university identifier?","Who controls identity, course membership, role overrides and retained history when sources disagree?"],"x":13148,"y":600,"width":2300,"height":1840}],"sectionHeights":{"Q1":3742,"Q2":2903,"Q3":2552,"Q4":2988,"Q5":2597,"Q6":1840},"rows":[{"ri":0,"id":"refero:91dab9ae-9676-49b6-8b26-01dde539cb0e","question":"Q1","sectionId":null,"y":500,"app":"Zendesk","source":"refero","evidenceType":"direct pattern","actor":"University IT","observed":"The SAML form requires a recognizable configuration name, SSO URL and certificate fingerprint. Helper text identifies the assertion-consumer URL and where to obtain certificate data. Optional logout URL and IP ranges follow; Save and Cancel end the form.","adaptation":"Give university IT provider-specific instructions beside each field and a recognizable connection name. A separate test and rollout preview would reduce uncertainty before institutional sign-in changes.","limitation":"One unfilled setup screen only. No connection test, save result, provider validation, group scope or provisioning lifecycle is visible. The proposed test is an adaptation, not an observed Zendesk step.","title":"Configure a named SAML connection","url":"https://refero.design/pages/91dab9ae-9676-49b6-8b26-01dde539cb0e","kind":"screen","take":"Explain every identity-provider value at the configuration field. Keep sign-in setup distinct from user provisioning, and add an explicit test before enabling institutional access.","stickyText":"Explain every identity-provider value at the configuration field. Keep sign-in setup distinct from user provisioning, and add an explicit test before enabling institutional access.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":1,"selectedStepIndices":[0],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Complete collected sequence: 1 step(s).","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"91dab9ae-9676-49b6-8b26-01dde539cb0e","label":"Create SAML configuration","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/zendesk-saml.jpg","relativePath":"assets/zendesk-saml.jpg","x":620,"y":574,"w":280,"h":204}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#refero:91dab9ae-9676-49b6-8b26-01dde539cb0e","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference refero:91dab9ae-9676-49b6-8b26-01dde539cb0e","h":326},{"ri":1,"id":"refero:4fc8ea47-ce2b-40b1-8817-71e138851fcc","question":"Q1","sectionId":null,"y":906,"app":"Calendly","source":"refero","evidenceType":"direct pattern","actor":"University IT","observed":"Organization Login has separate Single sign-on, User provisioning and Domain control tabs. The provisioning tab explains SCIM and provisioning/deprovisioning, marks Enterprise availability and offers help-center and Contact us routes.","adaptation":"Use distinct setup states for institutional sign-in and user lifecycle. Explain capabilities and prerequisites before requesting directory access, with a support path when integration needs IT involvement.","limitation":"This is an informational enterprise entry screen, not a working connection wizard. It does not demonstrate SCIM setup, scope selection, synchronization or deactivation results.","title":"Separate sign-in from user provisioning","url":"https://refero.design/pages/4fc8ea47-ce2b-40b1-8817-71e138851fcc","kind":"screen","take":"Place authentication and provisioning in separate admin areas, explaining that automated account creation and removal need their own setup and support route.","stickyText":"Place authentication and provisioning in separate admin areas, explaining that automated account creation and removal need their own setup and support route.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":1,"selectedStepIndices":[0],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Complete collected sequence: 1 step(s).","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"4fc8ea47-ce2b-40b1-8817-71e138851fcc","label":"User provisioning explanation and support entry","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/calendly-provisioning.jpg","relativePath":"assets/calendly-provisioning.jpg","x":620,"y":980,"w":280,"h":158}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#refero:4fc8ea47-ce2b-40b1-8817-71e138851fcc","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference refero:4fc8ea47-ce2b-40b1-8817-71e138851fcc","h":280},{"ri":2,"id":"mobbin:e304a20c-fb7b-467a-97de-7f725cd317c1","question":"Q1","sectionId":null,"y":1266,"app":"Remote","source":"mobbin","evidenceType":"analogy","actor":"university IT","observed":"Authentication settings opens a SAML explanation and numbered setup guide. IT copies the service-provider URL and audience into its identity provider, supplies company domain and identity-provider URL, and uploads a certificate. The final screenshot reports an unsupported certificate file type and lists accepted formats.","adaptation":"Give university IT a checklist for both systems, copy controls for app-provided values and explicit population scope. Explain invalid file formats next to the upload control before activation.","limitation":"The captured flow ends with a certificate-file error; no connection test, activation, successful sign-in, provisioning or group selection is shown. A company email domain is an observed SSO scope cue, not proof of university identity matching.","title":"Guide IT between the app and identity provider","url":"https://mobbin.com/flows/e304a20c-fb7b-467a-97de-7f725cd317c1","kind":"flow","take":"Number the configuration handoffs, explain which domains SSO affects, and validate certificate files at upload. Keep the setup state visible until the connection has actually succeeded.","stickyText":"Number the configuration handoffs, explain which domains SSO affects, and validate certificate files at upload. Keep the setup state visible until the connection has actually succeeded.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":4,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1,2,3],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Complete collected sequence: 4 step(s).","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex"