ed attributes with descriptions and enabled/disabled states. An edit dialog provides individual toggles and warns that changes to existing directory users may not appear immediately. After selected toggles are saved, the main table reflects the enabled attributes.","adaptation":"Preview the shared fields and default to the minimum institutional data needed. Explain optional fields and propagation timing before IT saves a change.","limitation":"This developer-admin example controls optional attributes rather than selecting directory groups. No actual user synchronization, failed update, legal permission or course-membership mapping is demonstrated.","title":"Choose which directory attributes are synchronized","url":"https://mobbin.com/flows/b7696e33-f9a3-406d-ac04-a210bd88cc1c","kind":"flow","take":"Let IT enable only the directory fields LearningSpace needs. Describe each field and disclose that changes to existing users may take time to appear.","stickyText":"Let IT enable only the directory fields LearningSpace needs. Describe each field and disclose that changes to existing users may take time to appear.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":4,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1,2,3],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Complete collected sequence: 4 step(s).","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"952b02f6-5679-4afe-8d31-04532d1e14a3","label":"Directory attribute list, all optional fields disabled","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/952b02f6-5679-4afe-8d31-04532d1e14a3.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/952b02f6-5679-4afe-8d31-04532d1e14a3.jpg","x":620,"y":1733,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":1,"originalStepIndex":1,"stepId":"dc451bfe-7fdc-435e-bd9f-5e8d6301d82d","label":"Edit dialog with propagation warning","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/dc451bfe-7fdc-435e-bd9f-5e8d6301d82d.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/dc451bfe-7fdc-435e-bd9f-5e8d6301d82d.jpg","x":916,"y":1733,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":2,"originalStepIndex":2,"stepId":"1ab66cfd-4a8d-47a9-a543-49eb64f35e0a","label":"Selected attributes enabled before Save","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/1ab66cfd-4a8d-47a9-a543-49eb64f35e0a.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/1ab66cfd-4a8d-47a9-a543-49eb64f35e0a.jpg","x":1212,"y":1733,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":3,"originalStepIndex":3,"stepId":"d31f7cc8-8f33-48b9-b1c1-3ee159a90f52","label":"Saved enabled/disabled states","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/d31f7cc8-8f33-48b9-b1c1-3ee159a90f52.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/d31f7cc8-8f33-48b9-b1c1-3ee159a90f52.jpg","x":1508,"y":1733,"w":280,"h":190}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#mobbin:b7696e33-f9a3-406d-ac04-a210bd88cc1c","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference mobbin:b7696e33-f9a3-406d-ac04-a210bd88cc1c","h":312},{"ri":4,"id":"documentation:entra-ldap","question":"Q1","sectionId":null,"y":2051,"app":"Microsoft Entra","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"Microsoft describes LDAP applications connecting to directory services. Its Entra example uses Domain Services and a one-way identity synchronization architecture, with networking and directory prerequisites.","adaptation":"Ask IT which directory and sign-in services exist before offering connection mechanisms. Explain authentication, provisioning, permissions, and course membership separately.","limitation":"Architecture documentation, not a setup flow. The Microsoft topology is one example and does not establish what LearningSpace supports.","title":"LDAP is a directory protocol","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/architecture/auth-ldap","kind":"screen","take":"Start with the university’s identity infrastructure. LDAP describes directory communication; it does not by itself provide app access or course membership.","stickyText":"Start with the university’s identity infrastructure. LDAP describes directory communication; it does not by itself provide app access or course membership.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:entra-ldap","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:entra-ldap","h":240},{"ri":5,"id":"documentation:okta-ad-scope","question":"Q1","sectionId":null,"y":2371,"app":"Okta","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"The AD integration settings separately select user and group OUs, delegated authentication, import schedule, username format, and matching rules. Documentation warns that changed filters can deactivate users or groups.","adaptation":"Show the selected population, shared attributes, and impact of scope changes before enabling a departmental rollout.","limitation":"AD-specific configuration. Okta’s LDAP feature table separately lists OU/container import filtering as unsupported; these connectors must not be treated as interchangeable.","title":"Select Active Directory users and groups before import","url":"https://help.okta.com/oie/en-us/content/topics/directory/ad-agent-configure-import.htm","kind":"screen","take":"Let IT select relevant organizational units and inspect import settings before bringing institutional users into the application.","stickyText":"Let IT select relevant organizational units and inspect import settings before bringing institutional users into the application.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:okta-ad-scope","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:okta-ad-scope","h":240},{"ri":6,"id":"documentation:google-simulation","question":"Q1","sectionId":null,"y":2691,"app":"Google Cloud Directory Sync","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"Google advises preparing LDAP data, running a simulated sync, and then running the full sync. It also recommends handling existing unmanaged accounts before synchronization and using focused search rules to exclude unwanted data.","adaptation":"Separate a read-only preview from applying changes. Ask IT to review account matches, excluded groups, and proposed removals.","limitation":"Text guidance only. A simulation does not demonstrate the institution’s authorization to transfer personal data.","title":"Simulate before the first live synchronization","url":"https://knowledge.workspace.google.com/admin/users/gcds-best-practices","kind":"screen","take":"Offer a real simulation before first sync so IT can verify the selected population and resolve existing unmanaged accounts.","stickyText":"Offer a real simulation before first sync so IT can verify the selected population and resolve existing unmanaged accounts.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:google-simulation","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:google-simulation","h":240},{"ri":7,"id":"documentation:entra-on-demand","question":"Q1","sectionId":null,"y":3011,"app":"Microsoft Entra","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"An administrator selects a user and starts provisioning. The result explains imported attributes, scope checks, matching, and action outcomes. A connection-test step appears only on failure. Missing matching attributes have documented recovery guidance.","adaptation":"Provide a representative-user diagnostic with understandable reasons for inclusion, exclusion, matching, and failure.","limitation":"This is a live provisioning operation, not a dry run. Official illustrations show selection and success, not every failure state.","title":"Test one user through provisioning diagnostics","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-provisioning/provision-on-demand","kind":"flow","take":"Trace one user through scope, matching, and the resulting action. Label this test clearly because on-demand provisioning can change the target account.","stickyText":"Trace one user through scope, matching, and the resulting action. Label this test clearly because on-demand provisioning can change the target account.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":2,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"2 selected official documentation illustration(s); not a live product session.","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"entra-on-demand:1","label":"Screenshot that shows the Microsoft Entra admin center UI for provisioning a user on demand.","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/entra-on-demand-0.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/entra-on-demand-0.png","x":620,"y":3085,"w":280,"h":149},{"i":1,"originalStepIndex":1,"stepId":"entra-on-demand:2","label":"Screenshot that shows the successful on-demand provisioning of a user.","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/entra-on-demand-1.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/entra-on-demand-1.png","x":916,"y":3085,"w":280,"h":149}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:entra-on-demand","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:entra-on-demand","h":271},{"ri":8,"id":"refero:4649","question":"Q2","sectionId":null,"y":500,"app":"Riverside","source":"refero","evidenceType":"analogy","actor":"Faculty / learner","observed":"From the marketing entry, the login modal offers a separate SSO link. The user enters a work email. The final screen says the email is not recognized for SSO and directs the person to their organization administrator; Back to Log in remains available.","adaptation":"Offer a clear university sign-in route alongside a separate guest route, with institution-specific support guidance when identity discovery fails. Treat this failure differently from successful sign-in without LearningSpace access.","limitation":"No identity-provider handoff, successful authentication, account creation, linking or course-access check is shown. Guest routing is a proposed adaptation. The first screen is a long marketing page retained only for complete sequence provenance.","title":"SSO email discovery with an explicit failure","url":"https://refero.design/flows/4649","kind":"flow","take":"Keep institutional sign-in recognizable and explain when an email cannot use it. Give a support route and return path without implying that authentication creates course access.","stickyText":"Keep institutional sign-in recognizable and explain when an email cannot use it. Give a support route and return path without implying that authentication creates course access.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":5,"selectedStepIndices":[1,2,3,4],"omittedStepIndices":[0],"sequenceNote":"Selected 4 of 5 steps; omitted original step(s) 1. Complete sequence: report.html#refero:4649","images":[{"i":1,"originalStepIndex":1,"stepId":"942168e6-2dfd-4a93-94d3-ee407c8e8966","label":"Login options with SSO link","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-4649/1.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-4649/1.jpg","x":620,"y":574,"w":280,"h":157},{"i":2,"originalStepIndex":2,"stepId":"2f7c207e-044f-4a8d-ae6c-2aa5da88ec07","label":"SSO work-email entry","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-4649/2.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-4649/2.jpg","x":916,"y":574,"w":280,"h":157},{"i":3,"originalStepIndex":3,"stepId":"59d24999-e4ee-4259-8723-be4aa5be3f74","label":"Email entered","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-4649/3.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-4649/3.jpg","x":1212,"y":574,"w":280,"h":157},{"i":4,"originalStepIndex":4,"stepId":"3775da7a-b67a-4c79-818f-b78dcffd8005","label":"SSO email not recognized; contact organization administrator","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-4649/4.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-4649/4.jpg","x":1508,"y":574,"w":280,"h":157}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#refero:4649","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference refero:4649","h":279},{"ri":9,"id":"mobbin:93a5db68-6f50-4b51-90fd-0b5ae39257a5","question":"Q2","sectionId":null,"y":859,"app":"incident.io","source":"mobbin","evidenceType":"analogy","actor":"faculty / learner","observed":"The login page offers Slack, Microsoft and SAML SSO. After an email is entered, an error says SAML login failed and suggests trying again or contacting the administrator. The sequence later shows the application home.","adaptation":"Distinguish institutional sign-in failure from an authenticated person lacking LearningSpace or course access. Keep the support route visible and make a separate guest route understandable.","limitation":"The intermediate successful authentication method is not captured between the SAML error and home. Do not interpret this sequence as successful SAML retry, account linking, first-login provisioning or no-application-access handling. Guest routing remains a proposal.","title":"Keep SAML failure and recovery routes visible","url":"https://mobbin.com/flows/93a5db68-6f50-4b51-90fd-0b5ae39257a5","kind":"flow","take":"Place a clear retry and administrator-support message beside failed institutional sign-in. A later app screen does not explain how the person authenticated or whether accounts were linked.","stickyText":"Place a clear retry and administrator-support message beside failed institutional sign-in. A later app screen does not explain how the person authenticated or whether accounts were linked.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":4,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1,2,3],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Complete collected sequence: 4 step(s).","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"d320f96d-739d-45ea-a4a7-8c8f92fcaf90","label":"Login options and SAML email entry","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/d320f96d-739d-45ea-a4a7-8c8f92fcaf90.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/d320f96d-739d-45ea-a4a7-8c8f92fcaf90.jpg","x":620,"y":933,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":1,"originalStepIndex":1,"stepId":"5ceb2f48-9668-421d-b59a-70da94d82a2e","label":"Email entered for SAML","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/5ceb2f48-9668-421d-b59a-70da94d82a2e.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/5ceb2f48-9668-421d-b59a-70da94d82a2e.jpg","x":916,"y":933,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":2,"originalStepIndex":2,"stepId":"e1843d29-60fa-4786-9191-b9704e17142d","label":"SAML login failed; retry or administrator guidance","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/e1843d29-60fa-4786-9191-b9704e17142d.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/e1843d29-60fa-4786-9191-b9704e17142d.jpg","x":1212,"y":933,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":3,"originalStepIndex":3,"stepId":"95e1a260-5034-4e86-82cd-04c17cd785fa","label":"Application home; successful authentication method not captured","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/95e1a260-5034-4e86-82cd-04c17cd785fa.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/95e1a260-5034-4e86-82cd-04c17cd785fa.jpg","x":1508,"y":933,"w":280,"h":190}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#mobbin:93a5db68-6f50-4b51-90fd-0b5ae39257a5","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference mobbin:93a5db68-6f50-4b51-90fd-0b5ae39257a5","h":312},{"ri":10,"id":"documentation:entra-matching","question":"Q2","sectionId":null,"y":1251,"app":"Microsoft Entra","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"Matching attributes connect existing source and target users. Entra evaluates configured attributes in precedence order until a unique match is found. Every user needs a value for at least one matching attribute; the target must support filtering on it.","adaptation":"Record institutional identifiers separately from display email, show matching provenance, and route collisions to an administrator.","limitation":"This does not prescribe a universal identifier. Ordered matching is not a compound match across several fields; target capabilities must be verified.","title":"Configure unique matching attributes and precedence","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-provisioning/customize-application-attributes#matching-users-in-the-source-and-target-systems","kind":"screen","take":"Agree on a stable identity match before creating accounts. Expose ambiguous or missing matches for review instead of assuming email is enough.","stickyText":"Agree on a stable identity match before creating accounts. Expose ambiguous or missing matches for review instead of assuming email is enough.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:entra-matching","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:entra-matching","h":240},{"ri":11,"id":"documentation:atlassian-jit","question":"Q2","sectionId":null,"y":1571,"app":"Atlassian","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"Atlassian documents first-login account creation through SAML SSO, verified-domain automatic claiming, linked domains, and an enforced default authentication policy. It warns that inconsistent IdP username and email settings can create mismatches or duplicates.","adaptation":"Make first-login provisioning a deliberate institutional policy and test how it behaves for an existing account.","limitation":"Official setup illustrations only; no end-user first-login completion is captured. This article is marked AI-generated by Atlassian. JIT alone does not demonstrate departures or access assignment.","title":"Create accounts at first SAML sign-in","url":"https://support.atlassian.com/atlassian-cloud/kb/what-is-just-in-time-provisioning-and-how-to-set-it-up/","kind":"flow","take":"Explain whether the account is created before login or at first sign-in. JIT needs explicit domain and policy configuration.","stickyText":"Explain whether the account is created before login or at first sign-in. JIT needs explicit domain and policy configuration.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":2,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"2 selected official documentation illustration(s); not a live product session.","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"atlassian-jit:1","label":"Automatically claim accounts from the verified domain","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/atlassian-jit-0.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/atlassian-jit-0.png","x":620,"y":1645,"w":280,"h":78},{"i":1,"originalStepIndex":1,"stepId":"atlassian-jit:2","label":"Require single sign-on in the default authentication policy","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/atlassian-jit-1.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/atlassian-jit-1.png","x":916,"y":1645,"w":280,"h":155}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:atlassian-jit","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:atlassian-jit","h":277},{"ri":12,"id":"documentation:github-linking","question":"Q2","sectionId":null,"y":1928,"app":"GitHub","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"GitHub members can link their IdP identity to an existing account. Administrators inspect the SAML identity link and can revoke an incorrect link so the member can retry. Session and credential revocation are separate actions.","adaptation":"Display link provenance and offer supervised relinking without suggesting that signing out or deleting the user is the same operation.","limitation":"The screenshot is a profile sidebar excerpt. The documented revoke-and-retry path is not visually captured end to end. GitHub’s organization model is an analogy.","title":"Inspect and repair a linked SAML identity","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud@latest/organizations/managing-saml-single-sign-on-for-your-organization/viewing-and-managing-a-members-saml-access-to-your-organization","kind":"screen","take":"Show which institutional identity is linked to an existing account, with a deliberate repair route when the wrong identity was connected.","stickyText":"Show which institutional identity is linked to an existing account, with a deliberate repair route when the wrong identity was connected.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":1,"selectedStepIndices":[0],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"1 selected official documentation illustration(s); not a live product session.","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"github-linking:1","label":"Screenshot of the people summary for @octocat. A link, labeled \"SAML identity linked\", is highlighted with an orange outline.","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/github-linking-1.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/github-linking-1.png","x":620,"y":2002,"w":280,"h":393}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:github-linking","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:github-linking","h":515},{"ri":13,"id":"mobbin:986b4b4a-9fa5-470e-92fb-ecb1ba4d7a1f","question":"Q3","sectionId":null,"y":500,"app":"Okta","source":"mobbin","evidenceType":"analogy","actor":"university IT / LearningSpace administrator","observed":"The directory route opens People with status filtering; later rows show Pending user action alongside Active. Groups has a Group source type filter, people and applications columns, an Everyone description, and an Okta Administrators group explicitly described as managed by Okta.","adaptation":"Expose source and lifecycle status for institutional users and groups. Explain system-managed membership and local exceptions, while representing each person’s course roles separately from institution-wide administration.","limitation":"This captures directory navigation and list states, not a continuous provisioning run. No externally sourced group is selected, controlled profile edit is attempted or course permission inherited. An Okta-managed administrator group is not evidence of university group synchronization.","title":"Show directory status and system-managed groups","url":"https://mobbin.com/flows/986b4b4a-9fa5-470e-92fb-ecb1ba4d7a1f","kind":"flow","take":"Distinguish pending people from active users and label who manages a group. Keep group source, membership counts and application assignments visible without equating them with course roles.","stickyText":"Distinguish pending people from active users and label who manages a group. Keep group source, membership counts and application assignments visible without equating them with course roles.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":5,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1,2,3,4],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Complete collected sequence: 5 step(s).","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"91368794-4b0a-44aa-8556-4865258940d3","label":"Directory onboarding context","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/91368794-4b0a-44aa-8556-4865258940d3.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/91368794-4b0a-44aa-8556-4865258940d3.jpg","x":620,"y":574,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":1,"originalStepIndex":1,"stepId":"02a533b3-ba02-4194-b5cb-5762d3d2b279","label":"Directory navigation expanded","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/02a533b3-ba02-4194-b5cb-5762d3d2b279.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/02a533b3-ba02-4194-b5cb-5762d3d2b279.jpg","x":916,"y":574,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":2,"originalStepIndex":2,"stepId":"9f98944b-93c9-4dc2-85f4-11f991d0545e","label":"People list with active status","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/9f98944b-93c9-4dc2-85f4-11f991d0545e.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/9f98944b-93c9-4dc2-85f4-11f991d0545e.jpg","x":1212,"y":574,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":3,"originalStepIndex":3,"stepId":"cc52905e-1f42-4fe7-984a-6a86f8271bc6","label":"People list with pending and active users","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/cc52905e-1f42-4fe7-984a-6a86f8271bc6.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/cc52905e-1f42-4fe7-984a-6a86f8271bc6.jpg","x":1508,"y":574,"w":280,"h":190},{"i":4,"originalStepIndex":4,"stepId":"2ae61b76-5411-42b1-87ec-3564bde6bd73","label":"Groups with source filter and Okta-managed administrator group","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/mobbin/2ae61b76-5411-42b1-87ec-3564bde6bd73.jpg","relativePath":"assets/mobbin/2ae61b76-5411-42b1-87ec-3564bde6bd73.jpg","x":1804,"y":574,"w":280,"h":190}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#mobbin:986b4b4a-9fa5-470e-92fb-ecb1ba4d7a1f","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference mobbin:986b4b4a-9fa5-470e-92fb-ecb1ba4d7a1f","h":312},{"ri":14,"id":"documentation:atlassian-managed","question":"Q3","sectionId":null,"y":892,"app":"Atlassian","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"Provisioned users and groups become available for granting app access. Synced groups are read-only in Atlassian and edited in the IdP. App access is granted through group assignment. External accounts have different attribute and deactivation behavior from managed accounts.","adaptation":"Show a source label and a reason beside controlled fields. Keep LearningSpace-specific access rules visible alongside inherited membership.","limitation":"Product and domain rules vary. The source has architecture diagrams, but no useful managed-profile screenshot was collected; diagram availability is not UI evidence.","title":"Separate directory ownership from application access","url":"https://support.atlassian.com/provisioning-users/docs/understand-user-provisioning/","kind":"screen","take":"Mark directory-controlled fields and groups, then explain the local access granted through those groups.","stickyText":"Mark directory-controlled fields and groups, then explain the local access granted through those groups.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:atlassian-managed","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:atlassian-managed","h":240},{"ri":15,"id":"documentation:github-team-sync","question":"Q3","sectionId":null,"y":1212,"app":"GitHub","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"An organization owner connects an existing team to IdP groups. Membership changes then come from the IdP, while repository access stays managed in GitHub. Team synchronization is not generally a service for provisioning new organization members.","adaptation":"Display both the membership source and local access assignments. Explain why a person in a directory group may still lack application access.","limitation":"GitHub teams are an analogy for LearningSpace groups, not course enrollments. Collected official images only show navigation, so they were omitted.","title":"External membership with local resource permissions","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud@latest/organizations/organizing-members-into-teams/synchronizing-a-team-with-an-identity-provider-group","kind":"screen","take":"Keep group membership ownership separate from resource permissions: directory teams can supply people while the application controls what the team accesses.","stickyText":"Keep group membership ownership separate from resource permissions: directory teams can supply people while the application controls what the team accesses.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:github-team-sync","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:github-team-sync","h":240},{"ri":16,"id":"documentation:atlassian-group-conflicts","question":"Q3","sectionId":null,"y":1532,"app":"Atlassian","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"When local and IdP groups share a name, Atlassian lists conflicts with app access and membership changes. Administrators review changes, adjust or rename IdP groups, and choose which groups to sync.","adaptation":"Make source conflicts reviewable and show the access consequences before transferring group ownership.","limitation":"The official image is an annotated table excerpt, not a complete flow. A shared group name should not be assumed to identify the same institutional population.","title":"Review access changes before replacing conflicting groups","url":"https://support.atlassian.com/provisioning-users/docs/resolve-group-conflicts-when-syncing-users/","kind":"screen","take":"Preview added and removed members alongside the access a conflicting group grants before replacing it with the directory version.","stickyText":"Preview added and removed members alongside the access a conflicting group grants before replacing it with the directory version.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":1,"selectedStepIndices":[0],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"1 selected official documentation illustration(s); not a live product session.","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"atlassian-group-conflicts:1","label":"A list of group names, their product access, and the changes that will happen with sync","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/atlassian-group-conflicts-0.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/atlassian-group-conflicts-0.png","x":620,"y":1606,"w":280,"h":113}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:atlassian-group-conflicts","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:atlassian-group-conflicts","h":240},{"ri":17,"id":"documentation:canvas-course-roles","question":"Q3","sectionId":null,"y":1852,"app":"Canvas","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"LearningSpace administrator","observed":"Canvas Enrollment objects include a user, course and section identifiers, role or role ID, and enrollment state. Its API can list enrollments by course, section, or user.","adaptation":"Store each person’s course relationships separately so the same institutional identity can have different roles in different courses.","limitation":"API structure establishes feasibility, not a tested UI or LearningSpace permission policy. Canvas custom roles require a validated mapping.","title":"Roles belong to course enrollments","url":"https://developerdocs.instructure.com/services/canvas/resources/enrollments","kind":"screen","take":"Represent role and status per course. A teaching role in one course should not silently become institution-wide administration.","stickyText":"Represent role and status per course. A teaching role in one course should not silently become institution-wide administration.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:canvas-course-roles","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:canvas-course-roles","h":240},{"ri":18,"id":"refero:1250","question":"Q4","sectionId":null,"y":500,"app":"Loom","source":"refero","evidenceType":"analogy","actor":"LearningSpace administrator","observed":"The Members list opens a member details panel with role, joined date, Active status and Deactivate. Confirmation explains lost workspace access, which shared content remains accessible, ownership constraints and reactivation billing. After confirmation, the active member count drops from two to one and an update toast appears.","adaptation":"Preview the effect on access, teaching history and retained learning records before a local deactivation. Keep deactivation separate from course enrollment removal and permanent deletion, and identify the system that owns the action.","limitation":"This is a local workspace action, not a directory-triggered departure. The flow does not show retained inactive rows, an actual reactivation, identity re-linking, synchronization or learning-record retention policy.","title":"Deactivate access while explaining content consequences","url":"https://refero.design/flows/1250","kind":"flow","take":"Before deactivation, separate access loss from historical-content consequences. State what remains available and confirm the person has left the active list.","stickyText":"Before deactivation, separate access loss from historical-content consequences. State what remains available and confirm the person has left the active list.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":4,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1,2,3],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Complete collected sequence: 4 step(s).","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"326fb4bf-ab76-4648-800b-b33c14b50e03","label":"Active workspace members","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-1250/0.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-1250/0.jpg","x":620,"y":574,"w":280,"h":168},{"i":1,"originalStepIndex":1,"stepId":"d3838abe-bd78-4da2-bbe3-05b3ba4c050e","label":"Member details and Deactivate action","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-1250/1.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-1250/1.jpg","x":916,"y":574,"w":280,"h":158},{"i":2,"originalStepIndex":2,"stepId":"892e7d52-3eab-48dd-8ea4-0027b9b9c6b1","label":"Deactivation consequences and confirmation","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-1250/2.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-1250/2.jpg","x":1212,"y":574,"w":280,"h":158},{"i":3,"originalStepIndex":3,"stepId":"3a135916-ba1c-4122-bcf5-696e6735cfdb","label":"Active list updated","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-1250/3.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-1250/3.jpg","x":1508,"y":574,"w":280,"h":158}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#refero:1250","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference refero:1250","h":290},{"ri":19,"id":"documentation:entra-lifecycle","question":"Q4","sectionId":null,"y":870,"app":"Microsoft Entra","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"Entra documents target disabling when users leave scope and deletion behavior depending on target capabilities. Restoring a soft-deleted user can reactivate the target account, while some group memberships need additional reconciliation. Failed individual operations are retried; widespread failures can quarantine the job.","adaptation":"Preserve identity links and learning history through deactivation. Show account state separately from course state and verify memberships on return.","limitation":"Connector behavior varies. The screenshots show configuration of disable/delete actions, not a completed returning-user journey.","title":"Separate disabling, deletion, and return","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-provisioning/how-provisioning-works","kind":"flow","take":"Disable access independently of deleting history, and define how returning users regain their account and memberships.","stickyText":"Disable access independently of deleting history, and define how returning users regain their account and memberships.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":2,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"2 selected official documentation illustration(s); not a live product session.","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"entra-lifecycle:1","label":"Disable a user","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/entra-lifecycle-3.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/entra-lifecycle-3.png","x":620,"y":944,"w":280,"h":124},{"i":1,"originalStepIndex":1,"stepId":"entra-lifecycle:2","label":"Delete a user","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/entra-lifecycle-4.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/entra-lifecycle-4.png","x":916,"y":944,"w":280,"h":124}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:entra-lifecycle","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:entra-lifecycle","h":246},{"ri":20,"id":"documentation:entra-status","question":"Q4","sectionId":null,"y":1196,"app":"Microsoft Entra","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"The provisioning status area distinguishes current initial or incremental cycles, synchronized user/group totals, last synchronization, and quarantine reasons such as invalid credentials. Logs can be searched using source or target user identifiers.","adaptation":"Separate last attempt from last success, explain stale data, and link operational status to affected records.","limitation":"The documentation uses an older Azure-branded status screenshot. Its specific timing and counts are illustrative, not service commitments.","title":"Show last completed synchronization and quarantine reason","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-provisioning/check-status-user-account-provisioning","kind":"screen","take":"Show the last completed sync, current progress, affected population, and failure reason so administrators can judge whether directory data is current.","stickyText":"Show 