or can resolve a specific identity problem with IT.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":1,"selectedStepIndices":[0],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"1 selected official documentation illustration(s); not a live product session.","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"entra-logs:1","label":"Screenshot of the download button in the provisioning logs.","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/documentation/entra-logs-0.png","relativePath":"assets/documentation/entra-logs-0.png","x":620,"y":1722,"w":280,"h":90}],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:entra-logs","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:entra-logs","h":240},{"ri":22,"id":"documentation:entra-deletion-guard","question":"Q4","sectionId":null,"y":1968,"app":"Microsoft Entra","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"Entra lets administrators configure a deletion threshold and notification address. Crossing the threshold quarantines provisioning. Administrators can inspect staged actions, explicitly allow deletes, or repair the source/configuration before restarting.","adaptation":"Treat a sudden reduction in the source population as a reviewable event. Keep last-known data and show why the job paused.","limitation":"The threshold also covers disables and is evaluated per cycle. This is documentation guidance; no relevant screenshot was collected.","title":"Quarantine unexpected mass removals","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-provisioning/accidental-deletions","kind":"screen","take":"Pause unusually large removals and let IT inspect the cause before changes are applied.","stickyText":"Pause unusually large removals and let IT inspect the cause before changes are applied.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:entra-deletion-guard","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:entra-deletion-guard","h":240},{"ri":23,"id":"documentation:atlassian-sync-actions","question":"Q4","sectionId":null,"y":2288,"app":"Atlassian","source":"documentation","evidenceType":"documentation","actor":"university IT","observed":"Atlassian documents targeted account sync and a separate stop-sync action. Stopping sync unlinks the account and removes SCIM group memberships while the account remains active. Multiple links disable the actions and require support. Success banners distinguish completed actions from failures.","adaptation":"Explain what a repair changes, confirm unlinking consequences, and retain the managed state until successful completion is known.","limitation":"Text-only evidence. These actions depend on account state and subscription; they do not establish a universally safe unlinking policy.","title":"Distinguish resynchronizing from stopping account sync","url":"https://support.atlassian.com/atlassian-cloud/kb/how-to-manage-account-sync-actions-in-atlassian-admin-hub/","kind":"screen","take":"Give stale data, wrong identity links, and unavailable recovery actions different explanations and next steps.","stickyText":"Give stale data, wrong identity links, and unavailable recovery actions different explanations and next steps.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":0,"selectedStepIndices":[],"omittedStepIndices":[],"sequenceNote":"Documentation evidence — no product screenshot.","images":[],"reportAnchor":"report.html#documentation:atlassian-sync-actions","reportPathLabel":"inspiration/university-identity/report.html — reference documentation:atlassian-sync-actions","h":240},{"ri":24,"id":"refero:671","question":"Q5","sectionId":null,"y":500,"app":"Intercom","source":"refero","evidenceType":"analogy","actor":"LearningSpace administrator","observed":"The CSV introduction states that matching user ID or email updates an existing person; otherwise it creates one. The flow maps CSV columns, previews mapped attributes, adds import tags and runs a background import. Its final screen shows 0 users created, 0 users updated and 9 invalid-email errors with row and column details.","adaptation":"For a Canvas export or other institutional CSV, require an explicit stable-identifier matching policy, preview additions versus updates, and provide actionable per-row validation. Preserve job history so administrators can correct and repeat a snapshot import.","limitation":"All nine rows fail in the observed run; this is not partial success. Successful duplicate resolution, recovery retry and a downloaded error report are not shown. The source metadata calls this a happy path, which the actual final screen contradicts. Email matching here is an analogy, not a recommended university identity key.","title":"Repeat-import matching and an all-error result","url":"https://refero.design/flows/671","kind":"flow","take":"Explain how repeat imports match existing people; report created, updated and failed rows separately. A finished job can still have zero successful records.","stickyText":"Explain how repeat imports match existing people; report created, updated and failed rows separately. A finished job can still have zero successful records.","counter":false,"stickyColor":"#A8DAFF","totalImages":13,"selectedStepIndices":[0,1,3,4,6,10,11,12],"omittedStepIndices":[2,5,7,8,9],"sequenceNote":"Selected 8 of 13 steps; omitted original step(s) 3, 6, 8, 9, 10. Complete sequence: report.html#refero:671","images":[{"i":0,"originalStepIndex":0,"stepId":"2e9768da-57ec-4142-9280-e6a630309675","label":"Choose CSV importer","path":"/Users/danielbrassnyo/Documents/dev-projects/elevate/essentials-2.0/inspiration/university-identity/assets/refero-671/0.jpg","relativePath":"assets/refero-671/0.jpg","x":620